soc: sunxi: add the H713 TVFE/TVCAP driver and hold the domains from boot

0096 put the node tvcap@50c0000 into the device tree, but its driver
stayed outside the tree (analyse/tvcap/h713-tvcap.c, cstenger's
EXPERIMENT patch 0087, carried as an out-of-tree module since 06.09.).
Every kernel built from the series therefore has a node without a driver
("sync_state() pending due to 50c0000.tvcap" in the HY300 Pro owner's
dmesg) and nobody on the ARM holds the TVFE and TVCAP power domains or
the capture clocks.

That is not only a matter of readable registers. The display firmware
(MIPS) detects an HDMI signal by polling its own HDMI-RX PHY at
0x06840000, which sits in the TVCAP domain, and raises its SignalChange
and HotPlug callbacks only when its port state machine reaches state 5.
That needs the domain powered and the capture clocks running at the
moment the source's TMDS edge arrives (analysis A13, sections 2, 5 and 8).
Measured on the HY310 without a source (hy310-cmp 19.09., 01-idle): the
INCAP total reads 0 and 0x0684037a gives a bus error - the domain is off.
The HY310's firmware generation still wins the race on a plug (02-plug:
three SignalChange callbacks, INCAP 1920x1080). The HY300 Pro's does not:
its PHY never passes the lock gate from a cold domain, no callback, no
capture, "no signal" although the audio locks (bridge session 18.09.,
logs 09 and 16: INCAP active 0, total 0x04650898). It worked exactly once
on that board, when the source was plugged right after boot while TVCAP
was still warm from the ARISC EDID/HPD sequence.

So the driver moves into the tree as drivers/soc/sunxi/sun50i-h713-tvcap.c
and is built in: CONFIG_SUN50I_H713_TVCAP=y in the board defconfig, so the
two domains and the four clocks are held from the first moment, before the
display and receive drivers (modules) load, and for the whole uptime.
The Kconfig entry is tristate with default m for arm64 sunxi - as a module
a hang on the first access costs a reboot instead of a reflash, which is
the safety cstenger's version did without; our defconfig says y.

The file is the out-of-tree module translated to English, reasoning kept,
with four deliberate differences: the reason it exists is now the warm
receiver (comment at the top); probe_read - the eight-word read of the
window after power on - defaults to off, because the read is a diagnostic
and not a product step (sun50i_h713_tvcap.probe_read=1 turns it on); the
two pm_runtime_get_sync() calls became pm_runtime_resume_and_get(), which
drops the usage count again when the resume fails, where the original
left it incremented on its error path; and a NULL from
dev_pm_domain_attach_by_name() - a node with fewer than two domains -
refuses the probe with -ENODEV instead of being dereferenced.

The device tree comment on the node said the driver was a module outside
the tree; it now says where it is and why it is built in. Nothing keyed on
a board or a firmware build: the node is in the SoC dtsi, the domains are
the SoC's.

Follow-up to 0096, which stays byte-identical.

diff -ruN a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
@@ -1534,16 +1534,17 @@
 		};
 
 		/*
-		 * TVFE/TVCAP-Inbetriebnahme. Ohne Strom auf diesen beiden Bereichen
-		 * haengt JEDER Zugriff auf ein HDMI-RX-Fenster den Bus -- ohne Abort,
-		 * ohne Watchdog. Beansprucht bewusst KEINEN Interrupt: tvtops
-		 * GIC_SPI 110 (hwirq 142) gehoert h713-afbd, am Geraet mit 615
-		 * Ausloesungen belegt. Und bewusst keine Panel-Eigenschaften:
-		 * tvtops panel_bl_en ist PB5, Hintergrundbeleuchtung UND Luefter.
+		 * TVFE/TVCAP bring-up. Without power on these two domains EVERY
+		 * access to an HDMI-RX window hangs the bus -- no abort, no
+		 * watchdog. Claims deliberately NO interrupt: tvtop's GIC_SPI 110
+		 * (hwirq 142) belongs to h713-afbd, proven on the device with 615
+		 * triggers. And deliberately no panel properties: tvtop's
+		 * panel_bl_en is PB5, the backlight AND the fan.
 		 *
-		 * Herkunft: cstengers Patch 0087, bei ihm am 02.09.2026 belegt.
-		 * Der Treiber ist bei uns ein Modul, nicht builtin -- siehe
-		 * analyse/tvcap/h713-tvcap.c.
+		 * Origin: cstenger's patch 0087, proven on his board 02.09.2026.
+		 * The driver, sun50i-h713-tvcap, is built in and holds both
+		 * domains and the four clocks from boot on: the display firmware
+		 * latches an HDMI signal only into a powered, clocked receiver.
 		 */
 		tvcap_bringup: tvcap@50c0000 {
 			compatible = "allwinner,h713-tvcap";
diff -ruN a/drivers/soc/sunxi/Kconfig b/drivers/soc/sunxi/Kconfig
--- a/drivers/soc/sunxi/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/soc/sunxi/Kconfig
@@ -39,3 +39,25 @@
 	  is not there yet when a built-in driver probes.
 
 	  If unsure, say N.
+
+config SUN50I_H713_TVCAP
+	tristate "Allwinner H713 TVFE/TVCAP power and clock bring-up"
+	depends on ARCH_SUNXI || COMPILE_TEST
+	depends on PM && OF
+	select PM_GENERIC_DOMAINS
+	default m if ARM64 && ARCH_SUNXI
+	help
+	  Holds the TVFE and TVCAP power domains and the TV capture clocks of
+	  the Allwinner H713 from boot on. The HDMI receiver, its PHY and the
+	  capture block live in those domains; while they are off every
+	  access to their windows hangs the bus, and the display firmware,
+	  which detects an HDMI signal by polling that PHY, cannot latch a
+	  signal whose TMDS edge arrives into a cold domain. Nothing else on
+	  the ARM holds them.
+
+	  Say y to hold the domains from the first moment, before the display
+	  and receive drivers load; that is the shipping configuration. As a
+	  module a hang on the first access costs a reboot instead of a
+	  reflash, which is why the default is m.
+
+	  The module will be called sun50i-h713-tvcap.
diff -ruN a/drivers/soc/sunxi/Makefile b/drivers/soc/sunxi/Makefile
--- a/drivers/soc/sunxi/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/soc/sunxi/Makefile
@@ -3,3 +3,4 @@
 obj-$(CONFIG_SUNXI_SRAM) +=	sunxi_sram.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_HY310_CPU_COMM) += cpu_comm/
 obj-$(CONFIG_SUN50I_H713_ARISC) += sun50i-h713-arisc.o
+obj-$(CONFIG_SUN50I_H713_TVCAP) += sun50i-h713-tvcap.o
diff -ruN a/drivers/soc/sunxi/sun50i-h713-tvcap.c b/drivers/soc/sunxi/sun50i-h713-tvcap.c
--- a/drivers/soc/sunxi/sun50i-h713-tvcap.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/sunxi/sun50i-h713-tvcap.c
@@ -0,0 +1,192 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
+/*
+ * sun50i-h713-tvcap.c -- hold the TVFE/TVCAP power domains and the TV
+ * capture clocks of the Allwinner H713 from boot on.
+ *
+ * Claims the two TV power domains and ungates the TV clocks so that the
+ * HDMI-RX windows become reachable at all. While both domains are off --
+ * and that is how the board starts -- every access to that address range
+ * hangs the bus, without an abort and without the watchdog noticing.
+ *
+ * Why this is built in and holds the domains for the whole uptime, not
+ * only while somebody reads the windows: the display firmware (MIPS)
+ * detects an HDMI signal by polling its own HDMI-RX PHY, which sits in
+ * the TVCAP domain, and it raises its SignalChange/HotPlug callbacks only
+ * when its port state machine has reached its locked state. That needs
+ * the PHY powered and the capture clocks running at the moment the
+ * source's TMDS edge arrives (analysis A13, sections 2, 5 and 8). Nothing
+ * else on the ARM holds the domains: measured on a HY310 without a source,
+ * the INCAP total reads 0 and the PHY window gives a bus error, i.e. the
+ * domain is off. The HY310's firmware generation still wins the race on a
+ * plug; the HY300 Pro's does not, and its receiver never latches a signal
+ * from a cold domain. Holding the domains from the first moment, before
+ * the display and receive drivers (modules) load, is what makes the edge
+ * land on a warm PHY on every board.
+ *
+ * Origin: cstenger's EXPERIMENT patch 0087 on the branch
+ * h713-display-video-path. Proven on his board (02.09.2026): after power
+ * on, the THDMIRX window reads structured values (+0x00 = 0x70f80029,
+ * +0x0c = 0xfe000115, +0x10 = 0x03ff00ff), genpd reports both domains
+ * "on", nothing else regresses. It ran as an out-of-tree module on the
+ * HY310 from 06.09.2026 (analyse/tvcap/); this is that file, in the tree,
+ * in English, with the domains held for the reason above.
+ *
+ * The read of the window (probe_read) is a diagnostic, not a product
+ * step, so it is off by default: whoever wants the proof that power and
+ * clock are what make the window readable boots with
+ * sun50i_h713_tvcap.probe_read=1 (or loads the module with probe_read=1).
+ * The reasoning behind that parameter has not changed: were the domains
+ * the whole explanation, data comes back; if the access hangs, the log
+ * ends exactly there and the next boot knows that power and clock are not
+ * enough.
+ *
+ * Do NOT take the vendor driver sunxi-tvtop for this: its node claims
+ * GIC_SPI 110 -- which our KMS driver holds for the AFBD -- and carries
+ * panel_bl_en = PB5, the backlight AND the fan. Neither may be touched to
+ * answer a read probe.
+ *
+ * Deliberately NOT here: no HPD, no EDID write, no PHY. The HPD pin lives
+ * at 0x07091014 and belongs to the ARISC (see doku/68); a read from the
+ * ARM hangs the SoC hard.
+ */
+#include <linux/clk.h>
+#include <linux/io.h>
+#include <linux/module.h>
+#include <linux/moduleparam.h>
+#include <linux/of.h>
+#include <linux/platform_device.h>
+#include <linux/pm_domain.h>
+#include <linux/pm_runtime.h>
+
+static bool probe_read;
+module_param(probe_read, bool, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(probe_read,
+	"read eight words of the THDMIRX window after power on (default: no)");
+
+struct h713_tvcap {
+	struct device		*dev;
+	struct device		*pd_tvfe;
+	struct device		*pd_tvcap;
+	struct clk_bulk_data	*clks;
+	int			num_clks;
+	void __iomem		*thdmirx;
+};
+
+static int h713_tvcap_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
+{
+	struct device *dev = &pdev->dev;
+	struct h713_tvcap *tv;
+	int ret, i;
+
+	tv = devm_kzalloc(dev, sizeof(*tv), GFP_KERNEL);
+	if (!tv)
+		return -ENOMEM;
+	tv->dev = dev;
+
+	/*
+	 * Two domains, so they cannot attach implicitly -- the implicit path
+	 * handles exactly one. Attach both by name and have the PM core keep
+	 * them on for the lifetime of this device. NULL means the node names
+	 * fewer than two domains: not this SoC's node, refuse rather than
+	 * dereference it.
+	 */
+	tv->pd_tvfe = dev_pm_domain_attach_by_name(dev, "tvfe");
+	if (IS_ERR_OR_NULL(tv->pd_tvfe))
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, tv->pd_tvfe ? PTR_ERR(tv->pd_tvfe)
+						    : -ENODEV,
+				     "cannot attach the TVFE domain\n");
+
+	tv->pd_tvcap = dev_pm_domain_attach_by_name(dev, "tvcap");
+	if (IS_ERR_OR_NULL(tv->pd_tvcap)) {
+		ret = dev_err_probe(dev, tv->pd_tvcap ? PTR_ERR(tv->pd_tvcap)
+						      : -ENODEV,
+				    "cannot attach the TVCAP domain\n");
+		goto err_detach_tvfe;
+	}
+
+	ret = pm_runtime_resume_and_get(tv->pd_tvfe);
+	if (ret < 0)
+		goto err_detach_tvcap;
+	ret = pm_runtime_resume_and_get(tv->pd_tvcap);
+	if (ret < 0)
+		goto err_put_tvfe;
+
+	ret = devm_clk_bulk_get_all(dev, &tv->clks);
+	if (ret < 0)
+		goto err_put_tvcap;
+	tv->num_clks = ret;
+
+	ret = clk_bulk_prepare_enable(tv->num_clks, tv->clks);
+	if (ret)
+		goto err_put_tvcap;
+
+	dev_info(dev, "TVFE+TVCAP powered, %d clocks enabled, held from now on\n",
+		 tv->num_clks);
+
+	if (!probe_read) {
+		platform_set_drvdata(pdev, tv);
+		return 0;
+	}
+
+	tv->thdmirx = devm_platform_ioremap_resource(pdev, 0);
+	if (IS_ERR(tv->thdmirx)) {
+		ret = PTR_ERR(tv->thdmirx);
+		goto err_disable_clks;
+	}
+
+	/*
+	 * The critical moment. Were the domains the whole explanation, data
+	 * comes back; if it hangs, the log ends exactly here -- and the next
+	 * boot knows that power and clock are not enough.
+	 */
+	dev_info(dev, "reading THDMIRX -- if this is the last line, it hung\n");
+	for (i = 0; i < 8; i++)
+		dev_info(dev, "  thdmirx+0x%02x = 0x%08x\n",
+			 i * 4, readl(tv->thdmirx + i * 4));
+
+	dev_info(dev, "THDMIRX window is readable\n");
+	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, tv);
+	return 0;
+
+err_disable_clks:
+	clk_bulk_disable_unprepare(tv->num_clks, tv->clks);
+err_put_tvcap:
+	pm_runtime_put(tv->pd_tvcap);
+err_put_tvfe:
+	pm_runtime_put(tv->pd_tvfe);
+err_detach_tvcap:
+	dev_pm_domain_detach(tv->pd_tvcap, true);
+err_detach_tvfe:
+	dev_pm_domain_detach(tv->pd_tvfe, true);
+	return ret;
+}
+
+static void h713_tvcap_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
+{
+	struct h713_tvcap *tv = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
+
+	clk_bulk_disable_unprepare(tv->num_clks, tv->clks);
+	pm_runtime_put(tv->pd_tvcap);
+	pm_runtime_put(tv->pd_tvfe);
+	dev_pm_domain_detach(tv->pd_tvcap, true);
+	dev_pm_domain_detach(tv->pd_tvfe, true);
+}
+
+static const struct of_device_id h713_tvcap_of_match[] = {
+	{ .compatible = "allwinner,h713-tvcap" },
+	{ }
+};
+MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, h713_tvcap_of_match);
+
+static struct platform_driver h713_tvcap_driver = {
+	.probe	= h713_tvcap_probe,
+	.remove	= h713_tvcap_remove,
+	.driver	= {
+		.name		= "sun50i-h713-tvcap",
+		.of_match_table	= h713_tvcap_of_match,
+	},
+};
+module_platform_driver(h713_tvcap_driver);
+
+MODULE_DESCRIPTION("Allwinner H713 TVFE/TVCAP power and clock bring-up");
+MODULE_LICENSE("GPL");
